1
00:04:26,086 --> 00:04:32,086
She has the best of both worlds... Now, she has to choose just one.

2
00:08:52,173 --> 00:08:58,173
Hannah Montana: The Movie is a comedy, drama,
family film directed by Peter Chelsom.

3
00:13:18,260 --> 00:13:24,260
When Miley Stewart (aka pop-star Hannah Montana) gets too caught up in the superstar
celebrity lifestyle, her dad decides it's time for a total change of scenery.

4
00:17:44,347 --> 00:17:50,347
But sweet niblets!

5
00:22:10,434 --> 00:22:16,434
Miley must trade in all the glitz and glamour of Hollywood for some ol' blue jeans on the family
farm in Tennessee, and question if she can be both Miley Stewart and Hannah Montana.

6
00:26:36,521 --> 00:26:42,521
Miley Stewart / Hannah Montana, played by Miley Cyrus.

7
00:31:02,608 --> 00:31:08,608
Robby Stewart, played by Billy Ray Cyrus.

8
00:35:28,695 --> 00:35:34,695
Lilly Truscott, played by Emily Osment.

9
00:39:54,782 --> 00:40:00,782
Ruby, played by Margo Martindale.

10
00:44:20,869 --> 00:44:26,869
Jackson Stewart, played by Jason Earles.

11
00:48:46,956 --> 00:48:52,956
Oswald Granger, played by Peter Gunn.

12
00:53:13,043 --> 00:53:19,043
Hannah Montana: The Movie is a 2009 American teen musical comedy drama film
based on the Disney Channel television series Hannah Montana.

13
00:57:39,130 --> 00:57:45,130
The film is produced by Walt Disney Pictures.

14
01:02:05,217 --> 01:02:11,217
Directed by Peter Chelsom and written by Dan Berendsen, the film stars series regulars Miley Cyrus, Billy Ray Cyrus, Emily Osment,
Moises Arias, Mitchel Musso and Jason Earles, as well as Lucas Till, Vanessa Williams, Margo Martindale and Melora Hardin.

15
01:06:31,304 --> 01:06:37,304
The film tells of how Miley Stewart's popularity and alternate celebrity persona begins to take over her life, so her father convinces
her to take a trip to her hometown of Crowley Corners, Tennessee to get some perspective on what matters most in life.

16
01:10:57,391 --> 01:11:03,391
Hannah Montana: The Movie is the second theatrical film based on a Disney Channel Original Series after The Lizzie McGuire Movie (2003), and is the second theatrical
release of the Hannah Montana franchise, its predecessor Hannah Montana & Miley Cyrus: Best of Both Worlds Concert being released a year prior in 2008.

17
01:15:23,478 --> 01:15:29,478
It is also the first, and so far only, theatrical film produced by It's a Laugh Productions and
Millar/Gough Ink, who is also known from producing the long-running hit series Smallville.

18
01:19:49,565 --> 01:19:55,565
Filming began in April 2008, much of it occurring in Columbia, Tennessee,
and Los Angeles, California, and was completed in July 2008.

19
01:24:15,652 --> 01:24:21,652
Hannah Montana: The Movie was released theatrically by Walt Disney
Pictures on April 10, 2009, in the United States.

20
01:28:41,739 --> 01:28:47,739
Despite mixed reviews, the film achieved commercial success, grossing $169.2
million worldwide against a $30 million production budget.

21
01:33:07,826 --> 01:33:13,826
The film explores themes of double life, countryside, pop star, musical, malibu.

22
01:37:33,913 --> 01:37:39,913
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
